---
/**
 * The mixed-signal path of the embedded FIR filter, typeset as an inline SVG.
 * Structure is from the repository: ISR-fed circular buffer, 32-tap FIR,
 * SPI DAC synchronized to the conversion rate, and coefficient banks held in
 * external EEPROM behind a checksummed UART protocol.
 */
---

<figure>
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 740 300"
    role="img"
    aria-label="Signal path diagram. Top lane: four analog inputs enter a scanning analog to digital converter driven from its interrupt handler, fill a circular buffer, pass through a 32 tap FIR convolution, and leave through a DAC over SPI synchronized to the conversion rate. Bottom lane: UART packets enter a packet queue, update coefficient banks, and the banks are stored in external EEPROM over I2C; the active bank feeds the FIR block."
    style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block;background:var(--paper);border:1px solid var(--rule)"
  >
    <defs>
      <marker id="fsd-arrow" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8 z" fill="var(--ink-muted)"></path>
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <g font-family="var(--mono)" font-size="12" fill="var(--ink)">
      <g font-size="10" fill="var(--ink-muted)" letter-spacing="1.5">
        <text x="20" y="28">SIGNAL PATH</text>
        <text x="20" y="188">COEFFICIENT PATH</text>
      </g>

      <!-- signal lane -->
      <rect x="20" y="42" width="104" height="44" fill="var(--wash)" stroke="var(--rule-strong)"></rect>
      <text x="72" y="60" text-anchor="middle">4 analog</text>
      <text x="72" y="76" text-anchor="middle">inputs</text>

      <rect x="164" y="42" width="110" height="44" fill="var(--wash)" stroke="var(--rule-strong)"></rect>
      <text x="219" y="60" text-anchor="middle">ADC scan,</text>
      <text x="219" y="76" text-anchor="middle">ISR-driven</text>

      <rect x="314" y="42" width="110" height="44" fill="var(--wash)" stroke="var(--rule-strong)"></rect>
      <text x="369" y="60" text-anchor="middle">circular</text>
      <text x="369" y="76" text-anchor="middle">buffer</text>

      <rect x="464" y="42" width="110" height="44" fill="var(--wash)" stroke="var(--rule-strong)"></rect>
      <text x="519" y="60" text-anchor="middle">32-tap FIR</text>
      <text x="519" y="76" text-anchor="middle">convolution</text>

      <rect x="614" y="42" width="106" height="44" fill="var(--wash)" stroke="var(--rule-strong)"></rect>
      <text x="667" y="60" text-anchor="middle">DAC over</text>
      <text x="667" y="76" text-anchor="middle">SPI</text>

      <!-- coefficient lane -->
      <rect x="20" y="202" width="120" height="44" fill="var(--wash)" stroke="var(--rule-strong)"></rect>
      <text x="80" y="220" text-anchor="middle">UART packets,</text>
      <text x="80" y="236" text-anchor="middle">checksummed</text>

      <rect x="200" y="202" width="110" height="44" fill="var(--wash)" stroke="var(--rule-strong)"></rect>
      <text x="255" y="220" text-anchor="middle">packet</text>
      <text x="255" y="236" text-anchor="middle">queue</text>

      <rect x="370" y="202" width="120" height="44" fill="var(--wash)" stroke="var(--rule-strong)"></rect>
      <text x="430" y="220" text-anchor="middle">coefficient</text>
      <text x="430" y="236" text-anchor="middle">banks</text>

      <rect x="560" y="202" width="140" height="44" fill="var(--wash)" stroke="var(--rule-strong)"></rect>
      <text x="630" y="220" text-anchor="middle">EEPROM over</text>
      <text x="630" y="236" text-anchor="middle">I2C, persistent</text>

      <!-- arrows -->
      <g stroke="var(--ink-muted)" fill="none" stroke-width="1.25" marker-end="url(#fsd-arrow)">
        <line x1="124" y1="64" x2="160" y2="64"></line>
        <line x1="274" y1="64" x2="310" y2="64"></line>
        <line x1="424" y1="64" x2="460" y2="64"></line>
        <line x1="574" y1="64" x2="610" y2="64"></line>
        <line x1="140" y1="224" x2="196" y2="224"></line>
        <line x1="310" y1="224" x2="366" y2="224"></line>
        <line x1="490" y1="224" x2="556" y2="224"></line>
        <line x1="600" y1="198" x2="530" y2="90"></line>
      </g>

      <g font-size="10" fill="var(--ink-muted)">
        <text x="540" y="150">active bank loads into the filter</text>
        <text x="20" y="130">output cadence is set by the converter, so the path is deterministic from sample in to sample out</text>
      </g>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    The two paths that never block each other: samples flow through the filter
    at the conversion rate while coefficient updates arrive asynchronously,
    survive power cycles in EEPROM, and swap in without a rebuild.
    <span class="figcaption__source">Source: repository ADC, filter, EEPROM and protocol modules.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>
